From 7a94b0792d76dca8ae10bf7a000f52e22ec434f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 09:40:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.5.0b: Traffic Analyzer Live (200ms) mode;
 diag-aware MCP advisor instructions

Traffic Analyzer: rtrafd base tick 1s -> 200ms (TICK_MS/TPS); WAN rate +
live.json publish 5x/s for the new "Live (200ms)" refresh option on
Reaper_Traffic.asp (RTRF_71, all 25 dicts; default stays 1s). Heavy
sources keep wall-clock cadence (per-class 2s, fcache/probe 5s); loop is
work-time-paced (CLOCK_MONOTONIC + nanosleep remainder) so heavy ticks
don't stretch the interval; quota check gated to 1/s; live.json "poll"
renamed "poll_ms"; RTRF_64 reworded (no longer "every second").

rmcpd: initialize instructions were static and always claimed read-only,
so the model undersold the consented diagnostics tier. Instructions now
branch on g_diag (affirmative "diagnostics ARE ENABLED, run the probes
yourself" vs "NO active diagnostics this session"); TOOLS_DIAG
descriptions reworded "Read-only probe" -> "Active probe; changes no
settings"; armed syslog logs read+diagnostics vs read-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
